{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the process for the election of a rector, it is necessary to begin with the rector's final year in their current position."
      ],
      "justification": "Initial trigger and first process step correctly aligned."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following this, the acceptance of proposals for candidates for the rector position should be launched."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the second step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once this is done, the rector can nominate themselves as a candidate for the position."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for self-nomination step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the nominations have been made, the acceptance of proposals should be stopped."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for stopping proposal acceptance."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a candidate meets the required criteria, they should be included in the list of candidates."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch opens XOR decision; guard and action faithfully capture the positive condition and outcome."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if a candidate does not meet the criteria, they should be informed of the refusal and the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard and action capture the negative condition, refusal notification, and early termination. End node matches process conclusion."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the list of candidates has been formed, it should be made public."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for publishing the candidate list."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, the candidates should promote their ideas to the public and organize a public meeting of the Academic Senate."
      ],
      "justification": "Single source step split into two sequential actions; behaviour fully preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The public meeting should then commence, ensuring that all members are able to vote for a new rector."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for meeting commencement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "converge:c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The public meeting should then commence, ensuring that all members are able to vote for a new rector."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural convergence point following preparatory/promotional steps before the meeting begins."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the meeting, an election should be conducted and the votes should be counted."
      ],
      "justification": "Source step split into two equivalent actions; ordering and behaviour preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the voting is successful, the result of the election should be announced."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guard correctly model the success condition leading to result announcement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n18",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the voting fails, another election should be conducted."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard and action correctly model the failure loop/repeat condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After announcing the result, the public meeting should be concluded and the candidate should be informed of the election results, marking the end of the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action covers concluding the meeting and informing the candidate; end node marks final process termination."
    }
  ],
